WEBVTT

00:00.230 --> 00:02.170
- What we're going to do in this video is

00:02.170 --> 00:06.130
talk about factors and factor pairs.

00:06.130 --> 00:07.730
Now when we talk about factors,

00:07.730 --> 00:10.780
these are really numbers that
can be multiplied together

00:10.780 --> 00:12.330
to make some number.

00:12.330 --> 00:16.710
So, for example, if I were
to talk about factors of six,

00:16.710 --> 00:21.710
I could multiply two
times three to get six

00:22.270 --> 00:27.190
and so we would say that two
and three are factors of six.

00:27.190 --> 00:29.480
In fact we would also
say that two and three

00:29.480 --> 00:32.190
is a factor pair for six
'cause when I multiply

00:32.190 --> 00:34.600
those two I can get six.

00:34.600 --> 00:37.160
Now to think about all of
the different factor pairs

00:37.160 --> 00:40.020
for a number we could think
about it in terms of area.

00:40.020 --> 00:43.500
How can we make a rectangle with area six?

00:43.500 --> 00:46.450
Well you could do it if it's
two units by three units.

00:46.450 --> 00:48.170
So it could look something like this,

00:48.170 --> 00:49.820
I'll just hand draw it.

00:49.820 --> 00:53.920
So let's say it has, so
let's say our rectangle

00:53.920 --> 00:55.460
looks like this.

00:55.460 --> 00:58.870
So it has two rows and then three columns

00:58.870 --> 01:00.910
and lets say these all have equal area,

01:00.910 --> 01:03.410
it's hand drawn but you
can see that the area here

01:03.410 --> 01:07.190
would be two times three,
which would be equal to

01:07.190 --> 01:09.160
six square units.

01:09.160 --> 01:14.160
Now, what if, what are other
ways to get to an area of six?

01:14.620 --> 01:18.410
Well you could have
something that is one row

01:18.410 --> 01:20.060
but then it has six columns.

01:20.060 --> 01:23.080
So maybe it looks something like this.

01:23.080 --> 01:24.490
It looks like this.

01:24.490 --> 01:29.490
So it's one row and then
you have one, two, three,

01:29.560 --> 01:33.570
four, five, and I want them all
to be roughly the same size.

01:33.570 --> 01:38.070
So it's one times six would
be also an area of six

01:38.070 --> 01:39.790
so that would be another factor pair.

01:39.790 --> 01:42.530
We know that two times
three is equal to six

01:42.530 --> 01:46.690
and we know that one
times six is equal to six

01:46.690 --> 01:50.150
and these are actually the
two factor pairs for six

01:50.150 --> 01:52.760
and we can do it with larger numbers.

01:52.760 --> 01:54.790
We could think about what
about all the factor pairs

01:54.790 --> 01:57.910
for something like 16?

01:57.910 --> 02:00.560
Pause this video and see if
you can think about that.

02:01.660 --> 02:04.910
Well I'll set up a little
table here to think about that

02:04.910 --> 02:08.900
and so in this column
I'll put the first factor

02:09.830 --> 02:13.890
and in this column I'll
put the second factor

02:13.890 --> 02:16.870
and the way I like to
do it is I start at one

02:16.870 --> 02:19.650
and I keep working up, up to the number,

02:19.650 --> 02:21.490
to try to figure out all of the factors.

02:21.490 --> 02:23.900
So let's start with one.

02:23.900 --> 02:26.300
So one is definitely divisible into 16

02:26.300 --> 02:28.020
and as long as you put
a whole number here it's

02:28.020 --> 02:30.030
going to be divisible by one
and we don't have to multiply

02:30.030 --> 02:34.120
by one to get to 16, we'll
have to multiply it by 16

02:34.120 --> 02:37.530
so that's a factor pair
right there, one and 16.

02:37.530 --> 02:38.520
Now what about two?

02:38.520 --> 02:40.840
Does two go into 16?

02:40.840 --> 02:43.660
Well sure, two times eight is 16 so

02:43.660 --> 02:44.770
that's another factor pair.

02:44.770 --> 02:47.070
Two times eight.

02:47.070 --> 02:48.800
We found another factor pair.

02:48.800 --> 02:49.710
Now what about three?

02:49.710 --> 02:53.140
Does three go evenly into 16?

02:53.140 --> 02:56.400
Well no, three times five is 15

02:56.400 --> 02:59.310
and three times six is 18
so three doesn't go into 16

02:59.310 --> 03:02.580
so three would not be a factor of 16.

03:02.580 --> 03:04.130
What about four?

03:04.130 --> 03:08.040
Well four times four is 16 so
that's a factor pair there.

03:08.040 --> 03:10.710
Four and four.

03:10.710 --> 03:12.180
What about five?

03:12.180 --> 03:15.510
Well no, five times two is
10, five times three is 15,

03:15.510 --> 03:16.970
five times four is 20.

03:16.970 --> 03:19.370
Five does not go evenly into 16.

03:19.370 --> 03:21.720
Same thing for six, six times two is 12,

03:21.720 --> 03:24.480
six times three is 18,
does not go evenly into 16.

03:24.480 --> 03:25.550
What about seven?

03:25.550 --> 03:27.610
Seven does not evenly go into 16.

03:27.610 --> 03:30.400
Seven times two is 14,
seven times three is 21.

03:30.400 --> 03:31.660
What about eight?

03:31.660 --> 03:34.180
Well we already know that
eight goes evenly into 16,

03:34.180 --> 03:36.170
you might be tempted to say
oh there's another factor pair

03:36.170 --> 03:39.370
of eight times two but we
already wrote that down.

03:39.370 --> 03:41.380
We just happened to say
that two is the first factor

03:41.380 --> 03:42.580
and eight is the second
factor but you could

03:42.580 --> 03:44.420
say it the other way around
so we don't have to then

03:44.420 --> 03:46.260
go to eight times two.

03:46.260 --> 03:49.640
And once you've gone half
way you can be confident

03:49.640 --> 03:51.650
that you've already found
all the factor pairs

03:51.650 --> 03:53.130
because then you could go to nine,

03:53.130 --> 03:58.130
nine doesn't go into it,
10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15

03:58.210 --> 04:01.210
but then 16, of course, is divisible by 16

04:01.210 --> 04:03.330
but we've already written
that here in this factor pair.

04:03.330 --> 04:04.940
So we have these three factor pairs,

04:04.940 --> 04:08.013
one and 16, two and
eight and four and four.
